    "text": "📍Panda Meister Westfälischestr 46, Charlottenburg: alright this was a bit of a trek for my east Berlin ass but that yu-xiang aubergine was honestly well worth it. And no matter what you do, don’t skip the dumplings. Never skip the dumplings 🥟 \n\nThanks a lot for the feast @Panda Meister Dumpling 🥰🥰 \n\n#berlinfood berlin vegan ",
    "subtitles": "I found a Chinese place in South London\nthat is both budget and veggie friendly.\nBut first, this is sunny.\nI have many hobbies and I am obsessed with food,\nso this is what I tried.\nI started with a dumpling in homemade chili oil.\nAnd did you see that price?\nWell, the taste was even better.\nI follow with this spicy bian bian hand pulled noodles.\nAnd look at the texture! How is this 8 90?\nI also tried this vegetable and glass noodle\nsteamed buns. It's a cross section for you.\nBut then I saw that they also offer vegan Mapo tofu.\nSo of course I had to try it.\nA tingling sensation. But the most unexpected was this overgrown dish.\nI wasn't planning to order it at first,\nbut the chef encouraged me to do it\nand it's all I've been thinking ever since.\nAfter that feast, I made use of my free will,\nordering Boba for dessert.\nAnyway, the place is called Panda Mia,\nand besides this venue in Charlottenburg,\nthey also have a kioski Osborne. Hope you like it.",
    "subtitlesLanguage": "eng-US",
